      "post_subject": "Photopolymer holo and some MBDCGs",
      "content_md": "Hi guys.\n\nA video of test transmission holo made using acrylamide-based photopolymer\n\nI took the recipe from \"Photopolymer holographic recording material\" by J. R. Lawrence, F. T. O’Neill, J. T. Sheridan\n\n7g PVA/70ml DI water\n\n8ml TEA\n\n2,4 g acrylamide\n\n0,8g bisacrylamide\n\n1ml 0,4% methylene blue\n\nup to 100ml with DI water\n\nI apply 3ml of this stuff on 5x5cm leveled glass plate.\n\nIt dries 2 days, requires high (60% or higher humidity) and 50mJ/cm^2. Besides its cost is much closer to $15/l than per ml \n\nAnd some of my MBDCG holos:\n\ngreetings\n\nAdam",
